# Step 28: script hooks, an extension's registered hooks on the loop's seam
# and on the session's own events (docs/steps/28/answered.md, points 2, 6
# and 8). Each rule of their run is broken here: on the seam beside the hook
# commands, given the event's object, heard as the loop hears a hook, their
# time from when they are asked, their run their own and stopped when it is
# let go, their host calls a hook's (no question, under the hook's name),
# nothing of them in a stopped turn, a stop of their own told, and only
# while their extension is loaded as approved.

[break] an-extensions-hooks-are-off-the-seam
rule: The hooks a loaded extension registered are on the loop's points beside the hook commands: the seam's `matching` gives them.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/hook_points.rs
find: matched.extend(self.scripts.matching(event, target));
replace: let _ = self.scripts.matching(event, target);
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::an_extensions_hook_is_on_its_event_and_its_answer_is_read

[break] an-extensions-hooks-are-put-on-no-event
rule: Registering a loaded extension puts the hooks it registered on their events.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/tools.rs
find: hooks.add(&loaded)
replace: { let _ = (hooks, &loaded); }
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::an_extensions_hook_is_on_its_event_and_its_answer_is_read

[break] a-hook-is-given-another-input
rule: A script hook's function is given the event's object, `HookInput::to_json`, as a hook command is given it on its standard input.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/script_hooks.rs
find: input.to_json()
replace: serde_json::json!({})
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::an_extensions_hook_is_on_its_event_and_its_answer_is_read

[break] a-hooks-failure-is-no-opinion
rule: A script hook that throws, or cannot run, has failed, which refuses where a hook gates.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/script_hooks.rs
find: HookRan::Failed(why) => Heard::Failed(failed(name, &why))
replace: HookRan::Failed(_) => Heard::Nothing
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::an_extensions_hook_is_on_its_event_and_its_answer_is_read

[break] a-hooks-answer-past-its-cap-is-heard
rule: A script hook's answer is at most 64 KiB of JSON, as a hook command's is: a larger one is a failure.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/script_hooks.rs
find: if size > MAX_ANSWER {
replace: if size > 1024 * MAX_ANSWER {
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::an_extensions_hook_is_on_its_event_and_its_answer_is_read

[break] an-observing-hook-is-heard
rule: A script hook registered with `observe: true` is an observer: never waited for, and its answer not read.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/script_hooks.rs
find: observe: definition.observe
replace: observe: definition.observe && false
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::an_extensions_hook_is_on_its_event_and_its_answer_is_read

[break] two-hooks-on-an-event-share-a-name
rule: An extension's hooks on one event are told apart by their names: the second on it is `<extension>/hook.<event>.2`.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/script_hooks.rs
find: let name = if *count == 1 {
replace: let name = if *count >= 1 {
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::an_extensions_hook_waiting_for_its_runtime_spends_its_own_time

[break] a-hooks-host-call-puts-its-question
rule: A hook's host call that the permission engine would ask about is refused, saying a hook may not put a question and naming the rule that would allow it: nobody is asked, so a hook runs only what the engine allows outright.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/host.rs
find: if self.phase == Phase::Hook {
replace: if self.phase == Phase::Evaluation {
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::a_hooks_host_calls_put_no_question
    cineris-core::it hook_commands::sys_a_hook_command_gates_replaces_fails_and_runs_past_its_time

[break] a-hooks-call-is-a-tools
rule: A script hook's call is a hook's (`Phase::Hook`): its host calls put no question, and it may not ask the user or write.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/tools.rs
find: phase: Phase::Hook
replace: phase: Phase::Tool
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::a_hooks_host_calls_put_no_question

[break] a-hooks-host-calls-are-decided-under-another-name
rule: A hook's host calls are decided under the hook's name, `<extension>/hook.<event>`, so that a rule about the extension (`deny ext probe/*`) reaches them.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/tools.rs
find: full_name: name
replace: full_name: "hook"
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::a_hooks_host_calls_put_no_question

[break] a-stopped-turns-hook-starts
rule: A script hook asked after its turn stopped does not start, as a hook command does not: nothing of it runs, and it is no stop of its own. A host call of one that did start is refused by the policy's stop all the same, so this is shown by a hook that makes none.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/script_hooks.rs
find: if policy.stopped_turn(turn_number(&self.turn)).is_some() {
replace: if policy.stopped_turn(turn_number(&self.turn)).is_some() && false {
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::after_a_stop_of_the_turn_its_extensions_hooks_run_nothing

[break] a-hooks-run-let-go-goes-on
rule: Dropped, a script hook's run's future stops it, even before its first poll: its call is withdrawn, and no runtime is made for it.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/script_hooks.rs
in: StopOnDrop::drop
find: self.0.cancel();
replace: let _ = &self.0;
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::an_extensions_hooks_runs_are_its_own_and_bounded

[break] a-turn-ends-hook-runs-past-its-cap
rule: A waited-for `turn.end` script hook has at most four runs going at once, as a hook command has: a fifth is not started, and says so.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/script_hooks.rs
find: self.running.load(Ordering::Acquire) >= TURN_END_AT_ONCE
replace: self.running.load(Ordering::Acquire) >= 1024 * TURN_END_AT_ONCE
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::an_extensions_hooks_runs_are_its_own_and_bounded

[break] a-withdrawn-extensions-hooks-stay
rule: An extension withdrawn from the session takes its hooks off their events with it.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/found/pipeline.rs
find: self.scripts.withdraw(&gone.1);
replace: let _ = &gone.1;
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::an_extensions_hooks_are_on_their_events_only_while_it_stands_approved

[break] an-extensions-session-start-hook-is-not-heard
rule: The `session.start` hooks of the extensions a session loads as it opens are heard before its first turn, each one's context a notice of the hook's.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/found/pipeline.rs
find: scripts.session_started(started, &*tell).await;
replace: let _ = (started, &tell);
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::an_extensions_hooks_run_as_its_session_opens_and_closes

[break] an-extensions-session-end-hook-does-not-run
rule: A session's extensions' `session.end` hooks run as it closes, beside its hook commands', within the same five seconds.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/hook_command.rs
find: let scripts = self.scripts.session_ending(session);
replace: let scripts = self.scripts.session_ending(session).into_iter().take(0).collect::<Vec<_>>();
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it extensions_hooks::an_extensions_hooks_run_as_its_session_opens_and_closes

[break] a-hooks-own-stop-is-not-told
rule: A stop that a script hook's own program's look at the protected paths makes is told to the user at once and holds back the next prompt, as a hook command's is.
os: linux
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/script_hooks.rs
find: self.commands.stopped(&self.name, &self.turn, note);
replace: let _ = note;
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it hook_commands::confined::sys_a_hooks_writes_are_confined_and_looked_at

[break] a-hooks-time-up-in-the-queue-stops-the-runtime
rule: A hook's call whose time is up while it waits for its turn is withdrawn before it starts, and the call the runtime serves goes on.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/engine/mod.rs
find: Event::Deadline if withdrawn(&claim)
replace: Event::Deadline if false && withdrawn(&claim)
caught-by:
    cineris-ext::it engine::a_hooks_time_runs_from_when_it_was_asked

[break] a-hooks-time-runs-from-its-start
rule: A hook's time runs from when it was asked: its deadline is what was left of its time when its call was sent, so that its wait for its turn counts.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/engine/mod.rs
find: cx.timer.sleep(cx.time.saturating_sub(waited))
replace: cx.timer.sleep(cx.time)
caught-by:
    cineris-ext::it engine::a_hooks_time_runs_from_when_it_was_asked
